  "notes": [
    "local failure-domain test: both groups are processes in one VM on one laptop",
    "the scheduler ran with --policy spread (spec D35), which splits the sessions evenly between the groups on every run: under the default policy the split depends on warm-pool refill and heartbeat timing, so the number of sessions lost with group b would vary from run to run",
    "kill command: scripts/cluster.sh kill-group b; affected sessions are those whose sandbox was on group b at the kill (ListSandboxes just before it)",
    "detection_ms is the kill -\u003e the first ListNodes (polled every 50ms until the observe window ends) that lists every node of group b as DEAD",
    "recovery_ms is the kill -\u003e the end of the last affected session's first successful request on a new incarnation (GetSandbox right after it shows an incarnation above the one at the kill), within the observe window",
    "each session starts one request, an Exec of print(1), every 200ms (later if the previous one took longer), each try with a 20s deadline; a try fails when its stream ends with a gRPC status, without an exit event, or with a non-zero exit",
    "a request is retried up to 3 times on Unavailable or DeadlineExceeded, after 1s and then twice the previous pause, and fails only if every try fails",
    "requests_failed counts failed requests that did not end before the kill; requests_failed_before_kill counts those that did",
    "requests_failed_unaffected counts failed requests, before or after the kill, of sessions not on the lost group; it must be 0 for a valid run",
    "max_blocked_exec_ms is the longest single Exec try; max_request_with_retries_ms is the longest request from its first try to its final outcome, retry pauses included",
    "exec_before_ms holds successful requests that ended before the kill and exec_after_ms those that started after it, each as the latency of the try that succeeded; requests_spanning_kill counts requests that started before the kill and ended after it, which are in neither series",
    "rescheduled counts affected sessions whose incarnation after the run is above the one at the kill",
    "lookup_errors counts failed GetSandbox and ListNodes calls; errors counts failed requests of unaffected sessions, lookup errors and failed destroys"
  ]
}
